// lib/data/seed_fixed_assets.dart
//
// Fixed (long-term, tangible) assets -- filtered from the full CDA Admin / CDA Ops
// inventory spreadsheets (cda_admin.xlsx, cda_ops.xlsx) down to items that are
// acquired for use in operations rather than resale and are expected to provide
// economic benefit over multiple years, per this definition:
//   Land, Buildings, Machinery, Vehicles, Furniture & fixtures,
//   Computers & office equipment.
//
// No Land, Buildings, or Vehicles were found in the source inventory sheets --
// only Furniture & Fixtures, Computers & Office Equipment, and Machinery &
// Equipment are represented below.
//
// NOT included here: ~320 small hardware/spare-part items (screw sizes, XT
// connector variants, propeller model numbers, tape/heat-shrink rolls, etc.)
// that are short-lived consumables rather than fixed assets -- these belong in
// seed_consumables.dart, not here. Also excluded: logbooks, documents, forms,
// and decorative/personal items, which are neither consumables nor fixed assets
// in the accounting sense and aren't meaningfully trackable as either.
//
// NOTE ON THE 'branch' FIELD:
// Each item's 'branch' holds the display label ("CDA Admin", "CDA Ops", or
// "CDA Ops & CDA Admin" for items shared across both) -- same convention as
// seed_consumables.dart / ConsumableService, so it plugs into the same branch
// filter pattern if reused for a Fixed Assets screen.
//
// 'category' holds the specific asset type ("Furniture & Fixtures", etc.) so a
// category filter can be built the same dynamic way as ConsumableListScreen's.

